{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PJx49t52XsSiDGKvhMBkqW","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.0-uc002-tac\n     2→title: \"Reverse lines of files via tac\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go tac binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary buffers\n     6→  all input, splits it into records on the separator, and writes the records in reverse\n     7→  order to stdout. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the\n     8→  Homebrew reference binary (gtac from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that\n     9→  their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd021-tac.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/tac.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go tac binary on a file or stdin.\n    21→      Example: printf 'first\\nsecond\\nthird\\n' | ./bin/tac\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/tac reads the entire input into memory, splits it into records on the record\n    25→      separator (default newline), and reverses the order of those records.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      cmd/tac writes the reversed records to stdout in order. When a custom separator\n    29→      (-s) is given, the separator is placed after (default) or before (-b) each record.\n    30→  - id: F4\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/tac and gtac\n    33→      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    34→  - id: F5\n    35→    step: |\n    36→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    37→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    38→  - id: F6\n    39→    step: |\n    40→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    41→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    42→\n    43→touchpoints:\n    44→  - T1: \"cmd/tac — full-input buffering, record reversal, separator handling (prd021-tac R1, R2, R3)\"\n    45→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    46→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    47→\n    48→success_criteria:\n    49→  - id: S1\n    50→    criterion: cmd/tac compiles and ./bin/tac exists after mage build.\n    51→  - id: S2\n    52→    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; lines are reversed, matching gtac byte-for-byte.\n    53→  - id: S3\n    54→    criterion: The differential test for input without a trailing newline passes; the last line (now first) has no newline.\n    55→  - id: S4\n    56→    criterion: The differential test for -s with a custom separator passes; records split on the given separator are reversed.\n    57→  - id: S5\n    58→    criterion: The differential test for -b with a custom separator passes; separators precede records in the output.\n    59→  - id: S6\n    60→    criterion: The differential test for multi-file input passes; each file is reversed independently.\n    61→\n    62→out_of_scope:\n    63→  - Files larger than available memory are not supported; tac buffers the full input.\n    64→  - Regex separator testing (-r) is covered but not the primary use case.\n    65→\n    66→test_suite: test-rel05.0\n    67→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abb2040a-f7c9-438c-b4c3-2eddab19244e","uuid":"c7fe6de0-dd7d-41f3-b84a-31c2d8c036d2","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/347/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.0-uc002-tac.yaml","content":"id: rel05.0-uc002-tac\ntitle: \"Reverse lines of files via tac\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go tac binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary buffers\n  all input, splits it into records on the separator, and writes the records in reverse\n  order to stdout. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the\n  Homebrew reference binary (gtac from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that\n  their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd021-tac.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/tac.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go tac binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: printf 'first\\nsecond\\nthird\\n' | ./bin/tac\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/tac reads the entire input into memory, splits it into records on the record\n      separator (default newline), and reverses the order of those records.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      cmd/tac writes the reversed records to stdout in order. When a custom separator\n      (-s) is given, the separator is placed after (default) or before (-b) each record.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/tac and gtac\n      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/tac — full-input buffering, record reversal, separator handling (prd021-tac R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/tac compiles and ./bin/tac exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; lines are reversed, matching gtac byte-for-byte.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for input without a trailing newline passes; the last line (now first) has no newline.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for -s with a custom separator passes; records split on the given separator are reversed.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for -b with a custom separator passes; separators precede records in the output.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: The differential test for multi-file input passes; each file is reversed independently.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Files larger than available memory are not supported; tac buffers the full input.\n  - Regex separator testing (-r) is covered but not the primary use case.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.0\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
